{"items":[{"recordId":"teach-generated-bd6d9f96545b3410","units":[{"role":"definition","basis":"common_knowledge","text":"Fan interaction denotes how a fan-shaped structure relates or communicates with the elements connected to it.","requires":[],"citationRequired":false}]},{"recordId":"teach-generated-f80cad9e237894ad","units":[{"role":"definition","basis":"common_knowledge","text":"Auxiliary port matching is the correspondence between supporting ports on related structures.","requires":[],"citationRequired":false}]},{"recordId":"teach-generated-ae6bb90f7da29a75","units":[{"role":"definition","basis":"common_knowledge","text":"An upward-rotated abstraction fan is an abstraction fan represented with its orientation rotated upward.","requires":["abstraction fan"],"citationRequired":false}]},{"recordId":"teach-generated-fd37daa3aed82649","units":[{"role":"definition","basis":"common_knowledge","text":"Auxiliary port order is the sequence in which supporting ports are arranged or identified.","requires":[],"citationRequired":false}]},{"recordId":"teach-generated-c08d4b1da7805f5c","units":[{"role":"definition","basis":"common_knowledge","text":"The first auxiliary is the supporting port occupying the first position in the auxiliary port order.","requires":["auxiliary port order"],"citationRequired":false}]},{"recordId":"teach-generated-42fffc3657069f75","units":[{"role":"definition","basis":"common_knowledge","text":"The second auxiliary is the supporting port occupying the second position in the auxiliary port order.","requires":["auxiliary port order"],"citationRequired":false}]},{"recordId":"teach-generated-55d5815d764e39b6","units":[{"role":"definition","basis":"common_knowledge","text":"A semantic port index is an identifier used to refer to a port by its meaning or role.","requires":[],"citationRequired":false}]},{"recordId":"teach-generated-db95a1b9878fd934","units":[{"role":"mechanism","basis":"common_knowledge","text":"Matching semantic port indices pairs ports